{
	title: 'Trust-gated project instructions and plugin session lifetimes',
	spec: 'Project trust is one explicit user decision covering AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md, project skills, and native Hal plugins. Ask before the first instruction injection or plugin activation only when applicable material exists, including /cd into such a project. Trust applies to the canonical project root and future content, not content hashes. The question offers Trust, Not now (default) and Never trust. Trust and Never trust persist in state/project-trust.ason; Not now saves nothing and skips project content in that tab until its next /cd, so a new tab or /cd there asks again. Pressing Enter on the default must never record a lasting refusal. Discover from the nearest Git root through cwd; outside Git use only cwd. Native project plugins live in .agents/plugins/hal and execute in the host with unrestricted in-process authority. Each directory stays active while any open tab needs it; when the last tab leaves or closes, deactivate its hooks and watcher and run cleanup. Reopening and host restart reactivate remembered trusted projects. Activation and deactivation remain ordinary hook points. Reconcile existing tab state rather than introducing a separate session-reference counter. Common durable forms carry trust questions in terminal and web. Prompt assembly, inspection and change notices must not bypass trust. Personal instructions and skills remain globally applicable. Existing Hal-home plugins and reviewed portable sync remain intact; project files do not enter that sync namespace. No new catalog or lifecycle event framework. Keep trust-boundary and lifecycle regression coverage for restart, concurrent tabs, cwd changes, newly appearing material, declined trust and canceled activation. Personal plugin discovery and sync are tracked separately.',
	status: 'done',
